{"assignees":[],"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Summary\n\nMake the Files view's `o` (`OpenDefault`: open with the OS default application) and `O` (`OpenWith`: type an application name) available in the Git view's file tree and in the PR diff window's file tree (#200).\n\n## Motivation\n\nIn the Git view and the diff window the only way to open the selected file is `e` (`$EDITOR`). Images, Markdown, design documents and the like are often better looked at in the default app or a browser, and switching to the Files view to find the same file again is a detour. Writing `\"o\" \"OpenDefault\"` in those `view` keys is silently ignored today (the handler lives only in `src/files/state.rs`), which is confusing config-wise as well.\n\n## Design\n\n- Move the `OpenDefault` / `OpenWith` implementation (`open_selected` and `OpenWithPrompt`: the input prompt, empty Enter / Esc cancel, the last app name remembered) out of `src/files/state.rs` into `core::ui` (or `core::open`), and have the Files view use that.\n- Add `\"o\" \"OpenDefault\"` / `\"O\" \"OpenWith\"` to the Git view (`page \"git\"`, `view` keys) and the diff window (`window \"diff\"`, `view` keys), calling the shared implementation from `handle_view_key`. The target is the selected `FileDiff`'s path joined to the working tree (in the diff window, the PR's worktree first when one exists, the same order as `e` from #201). A file that is not there is reported in the status bar (\"not in the working tree\").\n- The diff window's current `o` (the PR's Files tab in the browser) stays as `OpenBrowser` on another key, e.g. `g`, so `o` means the same thing in the Files view, the Git view and the diff window; the exact key is decided while implementing.\n- The help overlay (`?`) is generated from the keymap, so nothing to add there; the Config Reference's page `git` / window `diff` tables gain two rows.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `o` / `O` in the Git view's file tree behave as in the Files view (default app / typed app, status line, last app name remembered)\n- [ ] The same in the diff window, opening the file from the PR's worktree when one exists\n- [ ] The Files view is unchanged (its existing tests pass)\n- [ ] README / README.ja and the guide (Git view chapter, GitHub chapter, Config Reference en / ja) are updated\n- [ ] `tape/demo.tape` (Git view) or `demo-github-pr.tape` presses the keys and the GIF is re-recorded\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01N7wFSHbpTzvkK6WS1CRS7b","comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-10-23T10:32:24Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORNPWJs8AAAACXrzvTg","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"}],"number":204,"state":"CLOSED","title":"Git view and the diff window: `o` / `O` to open the selected file with the default app / a chosen app"}
